  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc16157 and the CD70 antigen through a series of target interactions. Npc16157 is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including Ebracteolatanolide A, 2-[(4bS,8aS,9S,10S)-1,9,10-trihydroxy-4b,8,8-trimethyl-3,4-dioxo-5,6,7,8a,9,10-hexahydrophenanthren-2-yl]propyl acetate, and Aconitic Acid, all of which are implicated in targeting the CD70 antigen. These findings indicate that Npc16157 may serve as a common intermediary in the biological pathways leading to CD70 antigen activation or modulation. The consistent presence of DNA polymerase eta as a target across these compounds suggests a possible functional role in the pathway, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence is robust, with similar scores across different paths, indicating a reliable pattern of interaction, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance.",
